From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: A733 enable eMMC HS400

Move the eMMC (mmc2) onto the sun60i-a733-emmc compatible so it binds the
HS400-capable cfg, and advertise HS400 (mmc-hs400-1_8v). max-frequency stays at
150 MHz: on this board a 200 MHz HS400 clock did not lock (every board test
-110'd or found no strobe window), so HS400 is first proven at the same 150 MHz
the eMMC already runs HS200 at, and raised only once 150 MHz is solid. The SD
node (mmc0) keeps sun60i-a733-mmc / sun20i-d1-mmc and is unaffected.

The chip is HS400-1.8V capable (EXT_CSD DEVICE_TYPE bit6, read on silicon) and
the data-strobe pin PC0 is already muxed in mmc2_pins. Not enhanced-strobe.

Depends on `mmc-sunxi-add-a733-emmc-hs400`; binding in `dt-bindings-mmc-allwinner-a733-emmc`.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -750,7 +750,7 @@
 		};
 
 		mmc2: mmc@4022000 {
-			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-mmc",
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-emmc",
 				     "allwinner,sun20i-d1-mmc";
 			reg = <0x0 0x04022000 0x0 0x1000>;
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_SMHC2>, <&ccu CLK_SMHC2>;
@@ -767,6 +767,7 @@
 			non-removable;
 			cap-mmc-highspeed;
 			mmc-hs200-1_8v;
+			mmc-hs400-1_8v;
 			cap-mmc-hw-reset;
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <0>;
